      "an_octopus_arm_has_thousands_of_sucker": "An octopus arm has thousands of suckers, each with up to 10,000 chemoreceptor cells. A single arm can taste more than your entire mouth + nose combined.",
      "an_octopus_has_a_beak_that_s_the_size_": "An octopus has a beak that's the size of its eye. It can squeeze through any opening bigger than the beak. What does this tell you about how its body is structured? Could you design a robot that does the same?",
      "an_octopus_mantle_can_contract_at_abou": "An octopus mantle can contract at about 0.2 m/s during a jet — by squid standards relatively slow. Squid mantle contraction during full jet can reach 0.8 m/s.",
      "an_octopus_the_size_of_a_grapefruit_ca": "An octopus the size of a grapefruit can squeeze through a hole the diameter of its eye (~2cm). The only rigid structure in the body is the chitinous beak.",
