      "the_iss_orbits_400_km_up_at_17_500_mph": "The ISS orbits 400 km up at 17,500 mph (28,000 km/h). It completes one orbit every 90 minutes — so astronauts see 16 sunrises + sunsets per day. ISS is the largest object humans have built in space.",
